1
00:00:00,171 --> 00:00:03,257
Only two countries made
more solar power than India.

2
00:00:03,421 --> 00:00:07,616
That's 2025 data from Ember,
compiled by Our World in Data.

3
00:00:07,808 --> 00:00:09,481
Rewind to 2015.

4
00:00:09,669 --> 00:00:14,308
Solar supplied just 0.54%
of India's electricity.

5
00:00:14,503 --> 00:00:18,356
Its solar plants generated about
7 terawatt-hours that year.

6
00:00:18,498 --> 00:00:23,571
By 2025, that had climbed
to about 196 terawatt-hours.

7
00:00:23,803 --> 00:00:27,563
Solar's share of India's
power rose to 9.4%.

8
00:00:27,808 --> 00:00:30,083
The only two countries ahead of India?

9
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:31,814
China and the United States.

10
00:00:32,125 --> 00:00:36,475
Still, coal produced about
71% of India's electricity,

11
00:00:36,475 --> 00:00:38,709
and renewables about 24%.

12
00:00:38,879 --> 00:00:41,435
Have you seen solar panels
spreading where you live?
